       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is three times the maximum labeled daily dose. No indication supports it, and it carries a high risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It would also give no more pain or anti-inflammatory benefit, because the effect plateaus well below that dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day), 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Help you get a second opinion.** If you think this patient needs something unusual, discuss it with your attending and a clinical pharmacist. They can verify the order through the proper channels.\n- **Look at other options.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter an adjunct such as scheduled acetaminophen.\n\nWhich would you like?"
